layout: layouts/feature.njk
wide: true
title: Email | Shellui
description: "Sign-in mail, event mail, newsletters, and broadcasts for every Shellui app. Pick a design, set rules per event, and send through your own provider."
eyebrow: Features
heading: "Send your product's email"
lede: "Sign-in links, event notices, newsletters, and announcements, all managed from Administration. Your team picks the designs and decides which events send mail."
---

<div>{% include "email-providers-visual-responsive.njk" %}</div>

<div class="mt-20 grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Email and webhooks, side by side</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Each service in Administration has an Email and webhooks page. Identity, storage, and hosting events are listed in one place, and you choose what each one does: send an email, call a webhook, or both.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">One event can send several emails, for example a welcome note to the new member and a notice to your team.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm">
    {% include "feature-visual-email.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="signin">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="signin" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Sign-in emails always go out first</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Magic links and invitations never wait behind a big newsletter or announcement. They arrive while the person is still on the sign-in page.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">A sign-in link goes only to the person who asked for it. Links can only point to your own domains, and you add the hosts you trust in Administration.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="templates">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="templates" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Start from a suggested email</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Each event comes with a suggested email in English and French, so a new rule sends something useful on day one.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Pick from 40 designs in five themes: Barebone, Matte, Protocol, Arcane, and Studio. Recolor any design with your Shellui theme, then edit it in a visual editor.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="translations">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="translations" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Write once, send in each language</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Add the subject and text for each language your team supports. Every recipient gets the email in their own language, and missing text falls back to your default.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="newsletters">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="newsletters" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Newsletters people choose to join</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Add a sign-up form to your site. People confirm by email before they join, and every email carries an unsubscribe link for that list.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Ask for extra details at sign-up, such as a company name for a demo request. Sign-ups, confirmations, and unsubscribes can each send an email or call a webhook, set per newsletter.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Import and export subscribers whenever you need to.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="broadcasts">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="broadcasts" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Announcements to the right members</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Send one email to members of your company. Pick the audience by group, role, access, join date, or last activity.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">{% include "email-visual-responsive.njk" %}</div>
</section>
<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="providers">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="providers" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Send through your own provider</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Each company connects its own Resend, Amazon SES, or SMTP account, and sends a test message before going live. Your keys stay encrypted.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Bounces and complaints come back from Resend, so Shellui stops mailing addresses that cannot receive mail.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="stats">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="stats" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-pretty text-foreground sm:text-3xl">See what was sent</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Administration shows email statistics, delivery status per message, and the health of scheduled jobs, so you know when something needs attention.</p>
  </div>
</section>

